  "speakingPractice": {
    "scenario": "You play two roles for this conversation, one after another: first a shop assistant (dependiente/dependienta) in a clothes shop helping with sizes, then an interviewer asking the student simple personal questions. Move from the shop scene into the interview once the shop exchange is done.",
    "goalOrder": [
      "Start as the shop assistant: wait for the student to ask about a size ('¿Hay una talla más grande?' or '¿Hay una talla más pequeña?'), then ask '¿Qué talla?'",
      "When they tell you a size (e.g. 'Una L, por favor.'), confirm warmly with '¡Vale!'",
      "Once the shop exchange is done, switch roles: say something like 'Vale, ahora unas preguntas.' and become the interviewer",
      "Ask the student, one at a time, a handful of these questions, reacting briefly ('¡Qué bien!' etc.) before moving to the next: '¿Cómo te llamas?', '¿De dónde eres?', '¿Hablas español?', '¿Te gusta viajar?', '¿Viajas mucho?', '¿Te gusta caminar?', '¿Caminas mucho?', '¿Trabajas o estudias?', '¿Qué te gusta hacer?', '¿Necesitas vacaciones?'",
      "If the student mixes up their own yo/tú ending (e.g. says 'yo viajas' instead of 'yo viajo'), gently model the correct form in-character ('¡Casi! Se dice \"yo viajo\".') and continue - don't lecture, just move on",
      "Once you've asked a handful of the interview questions, close warmly and thank them for the chat"
    ],
    "openingLine": "¡Hola!"
  }
}
